{"_id":"692479fd7c7d1fa20e767aa8","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"jV9oHJdtocQzzALylaFnA","description":"# Font Weight\n\nFont weight refers to the thickness or boldness of characters in a typeface. In CSS, it's a property that allows you to specify how heavy or light the font should appear. Values can be numeric (like 100, 400, 700) or descriptive (like `normal`, `bold`, `lighter`, `bolder`), offering control over the visual emphasis of text.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Font Weight","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-weight","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a6"},{"type":"article","title":"An Introduction to HTML/CSS Font Weight","url":"https://www.udacity.com/blog/2021/01/html-css-font-weight.html","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a7"},{"type":"article","title":"CSS font-weight Property","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/cssref/pr_font_weight.php","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a8"},{"type":"video","title":"CSS Tutorial For Beginners 30 - Font Weight","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qeh4UeaGTnc","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144a9"}],"createdAt":"2025-11-24T15:30:05.086Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","